  <!-- ============ CHIP TEXT ============
       2026-08-02 legibility pass #2 (user report: "its still hard too see the tags").
       FontSize 11 -> 13 on EVERY chip-text brush below. Every Fixed chip pill in
       GlobalChroniclePanelV2.xml was re-measured and widened in the SAME edit — see the
       arithmetic comment on the EVENT row there. The two rows now total 730px and 760px
       against an 852px budget, so both fit outright and no inter-chip spacing was
       surrendered. Colours are unchanged from pass #1 apart from ChipTextPicked (below).

       PASS #1 NOTES, STILL TRUE:
       FontSize 9 to 11 on EVERY chip-text brush below, and every colour lifted.

       WHY 9 EXISTED: the chip pills in GlobalChroniclePanelV2.xml are Fixed-width and were
       sized for 9pt. Gauntlet grid/stack cells here do NOT clip, so text that outgrows its
       pill paints straight over the neighbouring chip. Every pill was therefore widened by
       ~22% in the same commit — see the arithmetic comment on the EVENT row in the prefab.
       DO NOT raise these sizes again without re-widening the pills.

       THE COLOUR LIFT is a pure HSV VALUE lift: hue and saturation are held and only V is
       raised to ~0.92-0.94, so the category encoding (War red / Crime amber / Politics blue /
       Family green / Other stone) is untouched — every hue moved by less than 1 degree.
         #C89858 -> #EBB367   H 34.3 -> 34.5
         #CF9D92 -> #EBB2A6   H 10.8 -> 10.4
         #D8B884 -> #F0CC93   H 37.1 -> 36.8
         #A3BCD4 -> #B9D5F0   H 209.4 -> 209.4
         #AEC79A -> #D0EEB8   H 93.3 -> 93.3
         #C4B393 -> #EED9B3   H 39.2 -> 38.6
       On the #14100B chip that takes the unselected text from ~7.2:1 to ~10:1 contrast.

       EEChronicleChipText has three other consumers and all three GAIN from 11: the active
       year pill (whose INACTIVE twin already renders at 12 via EEChronicleYear, so 9 was the
       odd one out), and the 36px-tall VIEW IN ENCYCLOPEDIA call to action. Both are
       CoverChildren/StretchToParent-width, so neither can overflow. -->
  <Brush Name="EEChronicleChipText" Font="Galahad">
    <Layers>
    </Layers>
    <Styles>
      <Style Name="Default" FontColor="#EBB367FF" FontSize="13" />
    </Styles>
  </Brush>

  <!-- REPURPOSED 2026-08-02 (legibility pass #2). Name kept, meaning inverted.
       History: written in May as a DARK label for a SOLID GOLD picked pill, wired up earlier
       today, and rejected on sight — "ALl etc is blacked clicked etc". Near-black glyphs in
       Galahad at small sizes read as a smudge no matter what the contrast ratio says, and it
       was the only place in the panel that flipped the light-on-dark identity.
       NOW: the BRIGHT gold label for a DARK picked pill. The prefab's picked overlays no
       longer paint a gold fill at all; each one is a 2px gold frame around a lifted dark
       #3A2A18 body, and this brush is the text inside it.
       Measured on that body: #FFDCA8 on #3A2A18 is about 10.5:1, versus about 9.0:1 for the
       unselected #EBB367 on #241B12 — so the picked chip is the BRIGHTEST text in the
       toolbar as well as the only framed one, and nothing is inverted. -->
  <Brush Name="EEChronicleChipTextPicked" Font="Galahad">
    <Layers>
    </Layers>
